      "writtenOn": "2023-05-24T21:39:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you clarify if Wear supports Data saver mode or not? There should be two possibilities:\n- A device supports data saver mode: Then disable/enable data saver mode as needed in the tests.\n- A device does not support data saver mode: Then don\u0027t do any data saver related operations. \n\nThe current logic (with this cl) suggests that Wear does not support data saver mode, as the isDataSaverSupported() method returns false for Wear. However, we still want to be able to perform data saver-related operations, which IMHO is not correct.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 340,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 343,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "49eb710f2be521affab4a4be6a77ceb7797d78c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4725054_ed76abae",
        "filename": "tests/cts/hostside/app/src/com/android/cts/net/hostside/NetworkPolicyTestUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 343,
      "author": {
        "id": 1901791
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T08:08:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I know, Wear does not support Data saver mode. But some tests of `CtsHostsideNetworkTests` require `restrict background` to work.  aosp/2575912 to skip all these tests.\n\nI think Wear needs either this patch or aosp/2575912 to make  these tests pass.\n\nThanks,",
      "parentUuid": "9ff949f8_4953723c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 340,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 343,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "49eb710f2be521affab4a4be6a77ceb7797d78c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2757028a_713ab16a",
        "filename": "tests/cts/hostside/app/src/com/android/cts/net/hostside/NetworkPolicyTestUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 343,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101746
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T16:47:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As far as I know, Wear does not support Data saver mode\n\nThis seems to contradict the statement in http://b/279840893#comment2 that data saver mode is enabled by default.\n\n\n\u003e But some tests of CtsHostsideNetworkTests require restrict background to work.\n\nThis is true only if they support data saver. As you can see in this method, if the data saver is not supported, we return early and don\u0027t perform any data saver related operations.",
      "parentUuid": "b4725054_ed76abae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 340,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 343,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "49eb710f2be521affab4a4be6a77ceb7797d78c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07814b4e_86ee8ff8",
        "filename": "tests/cts/hostside/app/src/com/android/cts/net/hostside/NetworkPolicyTestUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 343,
      "author": {
        "id": 1901791
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-26T14:50:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per aosp/2046843, Wear should not be treated as support Data saver mode. And it is enabled by default. \n\nI would like to prefer aosp/2575912 instead of this.\n\nThe `setRestrictbackground` needs to work to make some tests pass. For example: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/android13-tests-dev:packages/modules/Connectivity/tests/cts/hostside/app/src/com/android/cts/net/hostside/AbstractExpeditedJobTest.java:\n\n```\npublic class AbstractExpeditedJobTest extends AbstractRestrictBackgroundNetworkTestCase {\n    @Before\n    public final void setUp() throws Exception {\n        super.setUp();\n        resetDeviceState();\n    }\n\n    @After\n    public final void tearDown() throws Exception {\n        super.tearDown();\n        resetDeviceState();\n    }\n\n    private void resetDeviceState() throws Exception {\n        resetBatteryState();\n        setBatterySaverMode(false);\n        setRestrictBackground(false);\n        setAppIdle(false);\n        setDozeMode(false);\n    }\n```\nsetRestrictBackground(false) is being called, which takes no effects, so, it causes some of tests of this class fail.",
      "parentUuid": "2757028a_713ab16a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 340,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 343,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "49eb710f2be521affab4a4be6a77ceb7797d78c4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
